R-GC5 R-CH17 R-CH13 R-CH9 R-CC10 R-GC11 (slice 243, Design Q612): `tln cache gc` and a user-channel build. The kind of the build is the nightly rule: the default stays, a build used in the last day stays, a build used in the GC age stays, an old build that nothing uses goes. The table of the channel does not matter (R-CH13: an installed build whose channel was removed is still a toolchain of that rule). No project is known, so the pins are not tested here (question G1 of the slice file). Run 1: dry run. Run 2: the real run. Run 3: a dry run with nothing to remove.
